# Brief

The objective asks us to improve the worker of `paper-repo` in completed research world `rw_e584f68c0d9c`. Its task was a one-paragraph report on how fast Mauna Loa CO2 rose over the last ten years, using NOAA annual means downloaded during the work. The target task requires downloading `https://gml.noaa.gov/webdata/ccgg/trends/co2/co2_annmean_mlo.csv`, keeping the downloaded file, and reporting in `report/report.md` one paragraph containing URL, fetch time, SHA-256, last year and annual mean, and ten-year average growth `(last year - year ten years earlier)/10`, with no figure.

The target world is complete and released (`rw_e584f68c0d9c`, final checkpoint `final-0e3e7fb9`, final release verified). Its positions were story-repo, paper-repo, internal-review-repo, and external-review-repo. The incumbent worker for each position was Codex with `gpt-6.1-sol` at low reasoning effort. The target completed in 13 turns and 417.3 model seconds; the final paper report and source data passed internal and external review.

For this round I will first establish evidence from the target monitor and records, then diagnose worker-specific failures against the task contract. Candidate runs must use the same model and agent, with only native settings/environment changed, and must be compared from identical starts under common judging. Priority is reliable source-data handling, exact arithmetic, preservation of requirements after context changes, and evidence-backed reporting. The world objective limits the experiment to one candidate and at most 8 turns/900 model seconds per run world.

What is not yet established: held-out diagnostic tasks and candidate configuration are owned by task-setter and tuner; incumbent/candidate run records and blinded judgements are not yet available. The target world’s release evidence shows success, so any diagnosis must distinguish latent worker weaknesses from world/position issues and avoid claiming a difference without matched runs.
